{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1200952-antitoxin-blood-vs-qietus","id":1200952,"title":"Antitoxin Blood vs Qietus","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-29T13:22:28-07:00","id":1200952,"title":"Antitoxin Blood vs Qietus","content":"In the Ravnos chapter of Lore of teh Clans is a 1 point merit named &quot;Antitoxin Blood&quot; that makes you immune against all supernatural poisons and toxins. And I was wondering if it would work against Quietus.<br /> <br /> How I would interpret it:<br /> <br /> - it should definitely work against Scorpion\u2019s Touch (Quietus 2)<br /> <br /> - against the V20 version of Dagon\u2019s Call (Quietus 3) it would probaly not work since that only requires to touch the target, but I'm not sure about the DAV20 Version were the traget need to ingest the Blood of the user<br /> <br /> - Baal\u2019s Caress (Quietus 4) I'm also not sure in the V20 version the stuff is called &quot;virulent ichor&quot; and not poison but they weapon it is put on are called &quot;poisoned&quot;, and in DAV20 it is directly called a acidic toxin<br /> <br /> - Taste of Death (Quietus 5) doesn't mention anything about poison, but if Baal\u2019s Caress is affected it should probably been to since DAV20 merges them anyway into one power<br /> <br /> - Baal\u2019s Bloody Talons (Quietus 7 V20) is called a &quot;blood-based poison&quot; and Blood of Destruction (Quietus 8 DAV20) &quot;virulent or acidic toxins&quot;, so they should also be affected if Baal\u2019s Caress is<br /> <br /> What do you think does Antitoxin Blood make you immune against all these Quietus powers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T07:02:47-07:00","id":1201240,"title":"","content":"Seems like an extremely powerful merit for one dot. I'll just retread some of your thoughts.<br /> <br /> Dagon's Call says absolutely nothing indicating poison, venom, toxin, etc. It is a concentration ability that constricts blood. So no defense there.<br /> Taste of Death just calls it 'caustic blood'. Still should work.<br /> <br /> I'd say the merit definitely works against Scorpion's touch as it is consistently called a poison.<br /> Baal's Caress turns blood into a 'virulent ichor'. It does use the term 'poisons' the weapon. And most telling, Baal's Bloody Talons says, &quot;The toxin generated by Baal\u2019s Caress is not enough to<br /> significantly harm some truly fearsome foes.&quot; So it acknowledges that Baal's Caress is a toxin, so the merit would work.<br /> It would also work against Baal's Bloody Talons given it not only is an advancement of that, but calls it a poison.<br /> Poison the Well of Life uses the term poison, poisonous, toxic shock, etc. Definitely is defended by the merit.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T07:32:52-07:00","id":1201249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1200952-antitoxin-blood-vs-qietus?p=1201240#post1201240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems like an extremely powerful merit for one dot. I'll just retread some of your thoughts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if you often fight against Assamites. There isn't much other stuff it works against, a few elder level Serpentis powers, Path of the Four Humours and probaly some more obscure Blood Magic stuff.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T07:35:32-07:00","id":1201250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1200952-antitoxin-blood-vs-qietus?p=1201249#post1201249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only if you often fight against Assamites. There isn't much other stuff it works against, a few elder level Serpentis powers, Path of the Four Humours and probaly some more obscure Blood Magic stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, even lower level Serpentis, because they get a venomous bite with Form of the Cobra. Anyway, any power that can just make one immune to a broad field of damage seems strong to me.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T08:32:28-07:00","id":1201280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1200952-antitoxin-blood-vs-qietus?p=1201250#post1201250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, even lower level Serpentis, because they get a venomous bite with Form of the Cobra. Anyway, any power that can just make one immune to a broad field of damage seems strong to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>That bite is iirc only poisonous for mortals.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T08:39:45-07:00","id":1201282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\